<article class="env-proposition" id="533E26">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/533E26">Proposition <span data-tag="533E26">3.2.2.7</span>.</a> Let $p: X \rightarrow \Delta ^ n$ be a Cartesian fibration. </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
There exists a composable sequence of maps 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \phi : A^0 \leftarrow A^1 \leftarrow \ldots \leftarrow A^ n  \]
</div>
<p>
 and a quasi-equivalence $q: M(\phi ) \rightarrow X$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Let 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \phi : A^0 \leftarrow A^1 \leftarrow \ldots \leftarrow A^ n  \]
</div>
<p>
 be a composable sequence of maps and $q: M(\phi ) \rightarrow X$ a quasi-equivalence. For any map $T \rightarrow \Delta ^ n$, the induced map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  M(\phi ) \times _{\Delta ^ n} T \rightarrow X \times _{\Delta ^ n} T \]
</div>
<p>
 is a categorical equivalence. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
